  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q:ai-database-access",
      "question": "Can Notion AI and agents read database content today, and read it well? The complaint in src:16 is from September 2024 and the product has shipped agents since.",
      "why": "It is the single sharpest objection in the AI pain and it may already be dead. Repeating a fixed objection in market-facing copy is worse than not mentioning AI at all.",
      "would_change": "If it is fixed, pain:paying-more-for-ai-i-dont-trust narrows to output quality and price, and the database angle flips into proof. If it is not, it stays the lead objection."
    },
    {
      "id": "q:offline-after-2025",
      "question": "Since the August 2025 offline release, does the pre-download requirement in src:6 still hold, or is offline now automatic for recently viewed pages?",
      "why": "pain:gone-when-the-network-is is currently evidenced by one post-release complaint and one pre-release data-loss story. The shape of the remaining gap decides whether this is a product pain or a perception pain.",
      "would_change": "If offline is now automatic, this becomes a 'people don't know' story for marketing rather than a product pain, and its confidence drops to low."
    },
    {
      "id": "q:who-owns-tidy",
      "question": "In a 50-300 person company on Notion, who actually holds the job of keeping the workspace tidy - ops, chief of staff, IT, or nobody?",
      "why": "Every ops-flavoured quote here is a practitioner improvising a governance practice, not someone whose title says workspace owner. The by_role targeting for pain:stale-and-duplicated depends on whether that role exists.",
      "would_change": "If there is no owner, the champion column is really a volunteer and the message has to reach them through their real job, not through an admin pitch."
    },
    {
      "id": "q:does-security-actually-block",
      "question": "Do enterprise security teams actually gate or disable Notion AI and agents, or is the disclosure criticism confined to a security-literate public and absent from real procurement?",
      "why": "pain:every-ai-feature-is-a-new-security-review rests on two Hacker News comments from one January 2026 thread. That is enough to raise it, not enough to size it.",
      "would_change": "Evidence from procurement or a named security review would raise confidence to high and make it a lead enterprise pain; absence would drop it to low and move it out of the main message."
    },
    {
      "id": "q:reddit-voice-missing",
      "question": "What do r/Notion and r/productivity say in their own words, especially the individual segment?",
      "why": "Reddit was unreachable during this pass, so the individual-segment evidence leans on Hacker News, which skews technical and towards people who left for Obsidian or plain files. The mainstream Notion lifer is under-represented here.",
      "would_change": "It would likely add a template-and-setup pain closer to the mainstream user, and could change the tone of pain:building-the-system-instead-of-using-it from regret to ongoing attachment."
    }
